  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "Which of the following is the negation of the statement: For all \\(x\\) of a certain set, \\(x^2\\gt0?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "For all \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\lt0\\)",
    "B": "For all \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\leq0\\)",
    "C": "For no \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\gt0\\)",
    "D": "For some \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\gt0\\)",
    "E": "For some \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\leq0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The claim that every member of a set satisfies a condition fails exactly when at least one member does not satisfy it. Thus “for all” changes to “for some,” with the same set understood.\n\nThe failure of \\(x^2>0\\) is \\(x^2\\leq0\\), including equality. Therefore the negation is: “For some \\(x\\) in the given set, \\(x^2\\leq0\\).” The answer is choice E.",
